# The source documents are EVIDENCE. Their bytes are hashed in docs/source-record.md and
# re-hashed on every build by gate:source-freshness, so a single byte of line-ending translation
# turns the gate red and the record into a lie about what we hold.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf = true. Git has been treating these
# PDFs as binary on its own — verified in three places (working tree, the committed blob, and a
# fresh clone, all 10 matching) — but that is git's content HEURISTIC, not a promise. One
# `*.pdf text` rule added later, or a platform whose heuristic decides differently, and the bytes
# move without anyone editing them.
#
# So it is stated rather than inferred. Evidence that can be silently rewritten is not evidence.
docs/sources/*.pdf binary
